  "reasoning": "The patient presents with vomiting, diarrhea, fatigue, abdominal pain, and most critically, yellow skin and dark urine. The yellowing of the skin (icterus) combined with dark urine are hallmark clinical signs of elevated bilirubin levels, which directly points to jaundice. Reviewing the provided training references, Reference [1] describes an almost identical symptom cluster (vomiting, tiredness, yellow skin, dark urine, abdominal pain) and correctly identifies the condition as jaundice. While other conditions like typhoid or malaria could explain the fatigue, vomiting, and abdominal pain, they do not account for the distinct yellow discoloration of the skin and dark urine. Therefore, jaundice is the definitive diagnosis supported by the facts.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]jaundice[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}

